      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Oh, sorry! I didn't mean to scare you with the goblin snack analogy, but you can't blame me for thinking about **goblin gardening** when a plant is looking so sad and mushy. It's like trying to feed a goblin a steak; they'd just get indigestion and turn yellow.\n\nYes, repotting is a great idea! If your current soil is too heavy or compacted, it's like trying to run through a swamp of **goblin slime**—the roots just can't breathe. You should switch to a mix with more perlite or orchid bark to improve drainage. Think of it as giving your Monstera a fresh pair of **goblin boots** so they can walk on dry land instead of sinking into mud.\n\nJust make sure the new pot has a big hole at the bottom, or the water will pool up and drown the roots again. It's like a **goblin's favorite trap**: if you don't have an exit, you're stuck in the water forever. With better soil and less frequent watering, your leaves should perk up soon.",
